# KTP camera capture + OCR suggestions

Sprint doc: `docs/sprints/revision-registration-ktp-camera-ocr-1.md`. Flag
`patient.ktp_camera_ocr` (default OFF).

1. **OCR output is a SUGGESTION, never data.** Nothing from OCR is written to a
   patient record without the operator ticking it, and the registration request
   refuses applied OCR values unless `ktp_ocr_verified` is accepted.
2. **OCR must not invent data.** Missing → null; invalid → null and not offered;
   below threshold / unknown confidence / glyph-corrected → offered but never
   pre-ticked; a label read twice differently → ambiguous, null.
3. **The NIK only cross-checks.** Never derive the birth date or gender from the
   NIK; a disagreement demotes both sides.
4. **Confident is not correct.** Measured: a lost space in a name came back as a
   confident read. Do not auto-apply "ok" values or remove the operator check.
5. **Only existing `mst_patients` columns are offered.** Fields without a column
   (birth place, religion, marital status) are display-only. Adding a column is
   a separate, explicit schema decision.
6. **OCR runs in the browser with SELF-HOSTED tesseract.js.** Worker, core and
   model come from `public/build/ocr/…` (copied by `vite.config.js`). Never let
   tesseract.js fall back to its CDN defaults; never send the image to an
   external OCR service without owner approval.
7. **The parse endpoint stores, logs and audits nothing**, answers `no-store`,
   and performs NO patient lookup — duplicates are detected at submit by
   `PatientRegistrationDuplicateCheck` (branch-scoped). Do not add a NIK
   existence check to it (it would become an enumeration oracle).
8. **OCR text is untrusted.** Bounded server-side; written to the DOM only via
   `.value` / `.textContent`.
9. **Image hardening:** the decompression-bomb guard reads the header BEFORE GD
   decodes; temp paths are rebuilt inside the caller's own folder; a retake
   discards only the same user's superseded temp image. A cleared or replaced
   photo is also DETACHED from the form so it is never archived under the
   patient being saved (rule 182 §2, AUDIT-PATIENT-KTP-ARCHIVE-PERSISTENCE-1).
10. **Rate limit** `ktp-scan`: per user AND per route — keep the two budgets separate.
11. Real-KTP accuracy and tablet latency are unmeasured until a supervised
    device trial; do not claim production readiness from synthetic results.
12. **Who may use it is decided by rule 178** (PHASE-1 supervised pilot): the
    flag alone enables nobody; `KtpCameraOcrPilotGate` is the single decider.
12. **How a value is READ is now governed by rule 179** (hybrid field-based OCR,
    REVISION-PATIENT-KTP-OCR-FIELD-BASED-ROI-1). Everything above about what may
    be offered and applied still holds.
13. **Nothing is read before the KTP holder agrees — rule 180** (PHASE-3, decision
    D7): the camera and OCR on any image source wait for an explicit "yes" to the
    approved wording, and the parse endpoint refuses text sent without it.
14. **How the card is lined up BEFORE capture is governed by rule 181**
    (REVISION-PATIENT-KTP-LIVE-FIELD-OVERLAY-OCR-1): a live field overlay on the
    preview, after the D7 "yes" only; OCR still runs once, after capture, and
    everything above about what may be offered and applied still holds.
